<title>UK: Hong Kong stocks in London slip on profit taking.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong stocks in London slip on profit taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong stocks in London edged lower on Monday after profit taking hit banking powerhouse HSBC Holdings, dealers said. But trading was quiet and the UK and U.S. markets failed to provide much direction.</p>
<p>HSBC was unchanged at HK$259 after dipping to HK$258.15.</p>
<p>The Hang Seng London Reference Index fell 14.23 points to 15,652.36 after showing a slight gain in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>A record-breaking performance by Hutchison Whampoa helped stocks in Hong Kong and London.</p>
<p>&quot;There really was no interest and today showed that we may be getting more into the summer doldrums,&quot; one London broker said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
